# Composer Flow Mode — Headless Widget Authoring [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

> Headless Pass 3. A headless widget becomes a first-class *logic node* you author in Flow: wire its ports, write each output's `expr` in the DSL, pick its schedule, add it to a runtime roster, push, and confirm it's alive. Almost nothing new in the graph model — the `kind="logic"` hook was placed ahead of need ([CXC-FL-HEADLESS]). Pre-vis (ratified): `ux/flow-headless-authoring-previs.v1.html`.

---

## 1. Intent

### [CXC-FLAUTH-INTENT] Author Logic Where You Author Displays

- definition: extend Flow mode ([SPEC:CXC-FLOW]) so a declarative headless widget ([SPEC:CXC-HEADLESS]) is created, wired, expression-authored, scheduled, and deployed as a **logic node** in the same node-graph as visual widgets and namespace hubs. The graph remains a *synced projection* of the `.compose.yaml` — edit in Flow / Bindings / Source, all stay in lockstep; Flow is not a new authority.
- closes: [CXC-HW-AUTHORING] (Flow mode is the headless editor) using the [CXC-FL-HEADLESS] forward hook.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

---

## 2. The Logic Node

### [CXC-FLAUTH-NODE] A Headless Widget Rendered as a Node

- model: a `FlowNode.kind="logic"` (hook already structural) drawn with a **λ** badge: **input ports** (left) = subscribed namespaces, **output ports** (right) = published namespaces, a **schedule badge** (∞ continuous / ⏱ periodic / ⚡ bus-triggered), and an expr/purpose summary. Title = widget id.
- prerequisite A — **static introspection** ([CXC-FLAUTH-INTROSPECT]): `build_graph` needs the headless widget's declared in/out ports + schedule, derived from its config (the analog of `bindable_attrs_for()` for visual widgets). No live runtime needed — this is design-time structure.
- prerequisite B — **first-class output wires** ([CXC-FLAUTH-OUTWIRE]): today publish wires exist in the model but only Button-class widgets author them. A logic node's outputs must wire to namespace hubs as first-class publish wires.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

### [CXC-FLAUTH-INTROSPECT] Headless Widget Static Introspection

- definition: a machine-readable table of a headless widget's ports + schedule, from its `.compose.yaml` (subscribed namespaces = inputs; `outputs:`/publish namespaces = outputs; the `headless.schedule` block = mode + interval/trigger). Mirrors the [CXC-BE-INTROSPECT] pattern (behavior/attr introspection) so `build_graph` and the inspector render from tables, not hardcoding.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

### [CXC-FLAUTH-OUTWIRE] Output Wires Become First-Class

- definition: generalize publish-wire authoring beyond Button-class — a drag from a logic node's output port to a namespace hub writes the widget's publish/`outputs:` entry into the `.compose.yaml`; the hub gains a publisher. Round-trips byte-identically; Bindings/Source reflect it.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

---

## 3. Authoring

### [CXC-FLAUTH-CREATE] Create & Wire

- create: a **＋ Logic node** affordance adds a new headless widget (named, empty ports, a default `continuous` schedule) to the design.
- wire inputs: drag a namespace hub (or a discovered rail signal) → a logic input port = subscribe (reuses existing drag-to-wire, [CXC-FL-MODEL] — no new mechanic).
- wire outputs: drag a logic output port → a namespace hub = publish ([CXC-FLAUTH-OUTWIRE]).
- multi-input rule (as-built 2026-07-10): the FIRST hub drop authors the `namespace:` subscribe; on a **bus-triggered** node further drops join the trigger list; on **continuous/periodic** nodes additional inputs are authored where they are consumed — as `ns()` reads inside the output exprs (the drop declares + selects the namespace). One node, many inputs, no special node-splitting.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

### [CXC-FLAUTH-EXPR] Expression Authoring (in the Inspector)

- surface: selecting a logic node switches the WC to the **Flow inspector** (already lens-following, [CXC-FL-SCALE]); it shows each output's `expr` in an inline editor, **live-validated by the DSL parser** ([SPEC:CXC-DSL] `dsl.try_parse`) — a green valid / red error state as you type. The **Source tab** remains the always-available raw escape hatch (the expr is just YAML).
- decision: expr is authored inline in the inspector per output, NOT a separate editor — the inspector is where the selected node is authored. Reuses the [SPEC:CXC-BINDEDIT] editor idioms.
- boundary: only the sanctioned `expr:` sites ([CXC-DSL-SITES]); arbitrary code stays refused ([CXC-BIND-BOUNDARY]).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

### [CXC-FLAUTH-SCHEDULE] Schedule Picker

- surface: a three-mode picker in the inspector — **continuous** (10 Hz daemon) / **periodic** (interval, editable) / **bus-triggered** (trigger namespace/pattern). Writes the widget's `headless.schedule` block ([CXC-HW-SCHEDULE]); the **schedule travels in the widget** ([CXC-HW-DEPLOY]), the roster stays pure membership.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

---

## 4. Deploy

### [CXC-FLAUTH-DEPLOY] Roster Assembly & Push

- surface: a **deploy card** — assign logic node(s) to a `runtime_id`; the card shows the roster path `bus://assets/headless/<runtime_id>.roster.yaml` and members; a **Push** action writes the roster + each widget config to bus_storage via the **Pass-1 loader** ([CXC-HW-DEPLOY], `BusStorageLoader` — no new deploy plumbing).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

---

## 5. Confirmation Tier (observability — in Pass-3 scope)

### [CXC-FLAUTH-CONFIRM] See It Run (the confirmation half of [CXC-HW-INTROSPECT])

- decision: the **Confirmation** half of observability lands here because its data is already reachable and it couples to surfaces built anyway; **Diagnosis** (tick trace / internal state) is Pass 4 ([CXC-HW-INTROSPECT]).
- **live port values**: a logic node's ports show current bus values when the widget is running — reuse the discovery liveness the hubs already have ([CXC-FL-DISCOVERY]). Zero new producer code; the node becomes a live readout.
- **runtime heartbeat**: the deploy card shows a runtime/roster health line (`hub-headless-01 · ✓ running · N widgets · last tick <age>`). Producer = a small periodic health publish from the headless runtime (a `_bus/headless/<runtime_id>/health` heartbeat) — the ONE modest runtime addition in Pass 3; it completes author→deploy→confirm.
- reserved for Pass 4: declare the `_bus/headless/<id>/*` namespace convention; the inspector carries a stubbed **"Inspect ▸"** affordance (no-op until the Pass-4 producer + Headless Monitor land). Design the node/inspector with a live-lane so Diagnosis layers on without special-casing.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]

---

## 6. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| CXC-FLAUTH-C1 | Logic node | A headless widget renders as a `kind="logic"` node with its declared in/out ports + schedule badge, from static introspection |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C2 | Static introspection | A ports/schedule table is derived from the `.compose.yaml`; `build_graph` + inspector render from it, no hardcoding |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C3 | Output wires first-class | Dragging a logic output port → hub writes the publish/`outputs:` entry; round-trips byte-identically; Bindings/Source reflect it |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C4 | Create & wire | ＋ Logic node adds a headless widget; input/output wiring uses existing drag-to-wire, no new mechanic |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C5 | Expr authoring | Inline per-output `expr` editor live-validates via the DSL parser (valid/error); Source tab shows the same YAML; arbitrary code refused |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C6 | Schedule | The picker writes `headless.schedule` (continuous/periodic/bus-triggered + interval/trigger); schedule travels in the widget |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C7 | Deploy | Push writes roster + widget configs to bus_storage via the Pass-1 loader; a headless runtime fetches + runs the roster |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C8 | Projection | Every Flow edit writes the `.compose.yaml`; Layout/Bindings/Source stay in lockstep; an Intelligence-authored widget yields the identical graph |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C9 | Live ports | A running widget's node shows live port values (discovery liveness) |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C10 | Heartbeat | The deploy card shows the runtime heartbeat (running / widget count / last-tick age) from `_bus/headless/<runtime_id>/health` |
| CXC-FLAUTH-C11 | Reserved seam | The `_bus/headless/<id>/*` convention is declared and the "Inspect ▸" stub exists (Pass-4 handoff) |

